{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":78,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:metric-preserving","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:metric-preserving","line":160,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Metric-Preserving Maps]\n\\label{def:metric-preserving}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nFor Riemannian manifolds with or without boundary, a map $\\varphi:(M,g)\\to(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$ preserves the metric when $\\varphi^*\\widetilde g=g$, equivalently\n\\[\n\\widetilde g_{\\varphi(p)}(d\\varphi_pv,d\\varphi_pw)=g_p(v,w)\n\\quad(p\\in M, v,w\\in T_pM).\n\\]\nEach $d\\varphi_p$ is then a linear isometry onto its image.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Metric-Preserving Maps] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6d65747269632d70726573657276696e67\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <p></p>For Riemannian manifolds with or without boundary, a map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varphi :(M,g)\\to (\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$\">$\\varphi :(M,g)\\to (\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$</span> preserves the metric when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varphi ^*\\widetilde g=g$\">$\\varphi ^*\\widetilde g=g$</span>, equivalently <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\widetilde g_{\\varphi (p)}(d\\varphi _pv,d\\varphi _pw)=g_p(v,w) \\quad (p\\in M, v,w\\in T_pM).  \\]\">\\[  \\widetilde g_{\\varphi (p)}(d\\varphi _pv,d\\varphi _pw)=g_p(v,w) \\quad (p\\in M, v,w\\in T_pM).  \\]</span> Each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\varphi _p$\">$d\\varphi _p$</span> is then a linear isometry onto its image. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:euclidean-metric","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:isometry","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:isometry","title":"def:isometry","label":"def:isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-immersion","title":"lem:metric-preserving-immersion","label":"lem:metric-preserving-immersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:isometry-symm","title":"lem:isometry-symm","label":"lem:isometry-symm"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-isometry","title":"def:local-isometry","label":"def:local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:metric-preserving-equidim-local-diffeomorphism","title":"lem:metric-preserving-equidim-local-diffeomorphism","label":"lem:metric-preserving-equidim-local-diffeomorphism"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:characterize-local-isometry","title":"prop:characterize-local-isometry","label":"prop:characterize-local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric","title":"def:covering-automorphism-invariant-metric","label":"de